Skip drogon's sqlite3_failed_commit test on Apple's system SQLite

The test, new in drogon 1.9.14, injects faults by registering a SQL
function with sqlite3_auto_extension(). Apple's system SQLite does not
support process-global auto extensions (its sqlite3.h deprecates
sqlite3_auto_extension on Apple platforms), so on macOS, where drogon
links /usr/lib/libsqlite3.dylib, the call fails and the test failed with
"Could not install SQLite fault injection".

On Apple platforms the test now exits with 77, which its ctest
SKIP_RETURN_CODE reports as a skip. Upstream drogon (master after
1.9.14) uses the same exit code to skip the test when the function is
not visible to drogon's SQLite; it still fails on Apple's system SQLite.
With another SQLite, such as Homebrew's, the call succeeds and the test
runs.

diff --git a/storage/ndb/rest-server2/extra/drogon/drogon-1.9.14/orm_lib/src/sqlite3_impl/test/CMakeLists.txt b/storage/ndb/rest-server2/extra/drogon/drogon-1.9.14/orm_lib/src/sqlite3_impl/test/CMakeLists.txt
index 66ffb53dde3..1a6078bded9 100644
--- a/storage/ndb/rest-server2/extra/drogon/drogon-1.9.14/orm_lib/src/sqlite3_impl/test/CMakeLists.txt
+++ b/storage/ndb/rest-server2/extra/drogon/drogon-1.9.14/orm_lib/src/sqlite3_impl/test/CMakeLists.txt
@@ -16,7 +16,9 @@ set_property(TARGET sqlite3_failed_commit_test PROPERTY CXX_STANDARD ${DROGON_CX
 set_property(TARGET sqlite3_failed_commit_test PROPERTY CXX_STANDARD_REQUIRED ON)
 set_property(TARGET sqlite3_failed_commit_test PROPERTY CXX_EXTENSIONS OFF)
 add_test(NAME sqlite3_failed_commit COMMAND sqlite3_failed_commit_test)
-set_tests_properties(sqlite3_failed_commit PROPERTIES TIMEOUT 30)
+set_tests_properties(sqlite3_failed_commit PROPERTIES
+                     TIMEOUT 30
+                     SKIP_RETURN_CODE 77)
 
 add_executable(sqlite3_disconnect_test Sqlite3DisconnectTest.cc)
 set_property(TARGET sqlite3_disconnect_test
diff --git a/storage/ndb/rest-server2/extra/drogon/drogon-1.9.14/orm_lib/src/sqlite3_impl/test/failed_commit_test.cc b/storage/ndb/rest-server2/extra/drogon/drogon-1.9.14/orm_lib/src/sqlite3_impl/test/failed_commit_test.cc
index d080ac580f8..c8ac81aac04 100644
--- a/storage/ndb/rest-server2/extra/drogon/drogon-1.9.14/orm_lib/src/sqlite3_impl/test/failed_commit_test.cc
+++ b/storage/ndb/rest-server2/extra/drogon/drogon-1.9.14/orm_lib/src/sqlite3_impl/test/failed_commit_test.cc
@@ -319,8 +319,21 @@ int main(int argc, char **argv)
     const auto entry = reinterpret_cast<void (*)()>(installFaults);
     if (sqlite3_auto_extension(entry) != SQLITE_OK)
     {
+#ifdef __APPLE__
+        // Apple's system SQLite does not support process-global auto
+        // extensions (sqlite3.h deprecates sqlite3_auto_extension on Apple
+        // platforms), so the faults cannot be installed. Report a skip
+        // (SKIP_RETURN_CODE in CMakeLists.txt) instead of a failure. With
+        // another SQLite, such as Homebrew's, the call succeeds and the
+        // test runs.
+        std::cout << "skipping: sqlite3_auto_extension() is not supported "
+                     "by this SQLite (Apple's system SQLite)"
+                  << std::endl;
+        return 77;
+#else
         std::cerr << "Could not install SQLite fault injection\n";
         return 1;
+#endif
     }
     const int result = drogon::test::run(argc, argv);
     sqlite3_cancel_auto_extension(entry);
